<title>USA: Arrow International Aug 31 Q4 net falls.</title>
<headline>Arrow International Aug 31 Q4 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>READING, Pa. 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.35		    $0.42</p>
<p> Net		 8,033		    9,799</p>
<p> Sales	     59,107		   57,612</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  23,229		   23,231</p>
<p>	  12   MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $1.41		    $1.52</p>
<p> Net		 32,831		   34,442</p>
<p> Sales	     229,945		  213,014</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  23,230		   22,684</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Full company name is Arrow International Inc.</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said the stronger U.S. dollar reduced the company's international sales by about $2.2 million in the fourth fiscal 1996 quarter. Overall, the stronger U.S. dollar reduced earnings an estimated $0.06 per share relative to the same period last year, it said in a statement.</p>
</text>
